# CLTS clears CR0.TS (bit 3); every other CR0 bit and all flags stay put.
# Real mode runs at privilege 0, so no #GP check applies here. When TS is
# already clear nothing changes, so the step retires without a CR0 write.
read_msw status
bit ts status 3
not clear ts
retire_if clear
const keep 16 65527
and cleared status keep
zext value cleared 32
write_control 0 value
preserve_flags all
retire
